<section class="section">
  <div class="shell about-narrative">
    <p class="section-index">The story so far</p>
    <div class="story-chapter"><span>2017</span><div><h2>I started Upstack Studio.</h2><p>For years, my team and I built web and mobile products with business owners. We saw what customers needed, what teams could use and why some projects worked while others did not.</p><p>It taught me a simple lesson: knowing what to build matters more than knowing how to build it.</p></div></div>
    <figure class="wide-story-photo"><img src="/assets/images/adrian/upstack-team.webp" alt="Adrian Ching with the Upstack Studio team" loading="lazy" width="1130" height="1130"><figcaption>The Upstack Studio team.</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="story-chapter"><span>Then</span><div><h2>I chose to close the agency.</h2><p>The work still had value, but it was no longer the business I wanted to spend the next ten years building. I wanted to own the products, own the results and focus on fewer, bigger ideas.</p><p>It was not a dramatic ending. It was simply the right choice.</p></div></div>
    <div class="story-chapter"><span>Now</span><div><h2>AI changed how I think about building.</h2><p>Software is getting faster and cheaper to make. That means the real value is in finding the right problem, knowing the customer and choosing what is worth building.</p><p>Small teams can now do much more. They can also waste money much faster. Clear thinking matters more than ever.</p></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-dark" id="what-im-building">
  <div class="shell about-build-grid">
    <div><p class="section-index">What I’m building</p><h2>One main company.<br>More to come.</h2></div>
    <div class="build-ambition"><span>01</span><h3>Second Team</h3><p>Second Team is my main company and where most of my time goes. We are building a better way for businesses to find growth opportunities and act on them.</p><p>I’ll share what I learn, while keeping private product work private.</p></div>
    <div class="build-ambition"><span>02</span><h3>My own products</h3><p>Over time, I want to build and own a group of useful software products, media and online businesses.</p><p>This website is where I’ll share that work.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell values-grid">
    <div><p class="section-index">How I try to work</p><h2>Useful over impressive.</h2></div>
    <div class="values-list"><p><span>01</span>Start with the business problem, not the tool.</p><p><span>02</span>Tell the truth, even when the answer is “don’t build it.”</p><p><span>03</span>Do fewer things and do them well.</p><p><span>04</span>Share lessons from real work.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

